# ops.env - settings for the scripts in /opt/bonanza/ops.
#
# Copy to /opt/bonanza/ops.env and keep it private:
#   install -m 600 ops.env.example /opt/bonanza/ops.env
# (systemd/install.sh does this for you if the file does not exist yet.)
#
# Format: plain shell, KEY=value, one per line, no spaces around "=". Quote a
# value that contains spaces or special characters. Every line below is
# optional; a commented-out line shows the default.
#
# This example contains no real values.

# ── Alerts (healthwatch.sh) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Where alerts are POSTed as JSON. Treat the URL as a secret: anyone who has
# it can post to your channel. Leave empty to only log to the journal.
#   Slack:    the incoming-webhook URL
#   Discord:  the webhook URL
#   ntfy:     the SERVER ROOT, for example https://ntfy.sh  (not the topic URL),
#             and set ALERT_NTFY_TOPIC below
# Check delivery with: /opt/bonanza/ops/healthwatch.sh --test-alert
ALERT_WEBHOOK_URL=

# ntfy only: the topic to publish to. Pick a long random name; on a public
# ntfy server, anyone who knows the topic name can read it.
ALERT_NTFY_TOPIC=

# Label at the start of every alert title.
# ALERT_NAME=bonanza

# Hours between reminders while a problem stays open.
# ALERT_REMINDER_HOURS=24

# Seconds to wait for the webhook to answer.
# ALERT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=15

# ── Thresholds (healthwatch.sh) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# Disk usage in percent: warning and critical.
# DISK_WARN_PCT=80
# DISK_CRIT_PCT=90

# Paths whose filesystems are checked, separated by spaces. Empty = "/" and
# Docker's data directory.
# DISK_PATHS=

# Alert when the last successful backup is older than this many hours. The
# backup runs daily, so 26 leaves two hours of slack.
# BACKUP_MAX_AGE_HOURS=26

# Alert when the last successful restore verification is older than this many
# days. It runs weekly, so 8 leaves one day of slack.
# RESTORE_VERIFY_MAX_AGE_DAYS=8

# Alert when less than this many MB of memory is available.
# MEM_MIN_AVAILABLE_MB=1024

# Alert when a required reboot has been pending for longer than this many
# hours (it should happen by itself at 03:30).
# REBOOT_PENDING_MAX_HOURS=26

# ── Deployment (deploy.sh, rollback.sh, restore.sh) ──────────────────────────

# Seconds to wait for every service to report healthy after a deployment or a
# rollback, before the attempt counts as failed.
# DEPLOY_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=300

# Seconds to wait for the stack after a database restore.
# RESTORE_HEALTH_TIMEOUT=300

# Name of the one-shot Compose service that runs database migrations.
# MIGRATE_SERVICE=migrate

# Services stopped while restore.sh replaces the database.
# APP_SERVICES="medusa-server medusa-worker storefront"

# ── Paths (change only for testing away from the VM) ─────────────────────────

# BONANZA_STATE_DIR=/opt/bonanza/state
# BONANZA_TMP_DIR=/opt/bonanza/tmp
# BONANZA_COMPOSE_FILE=/opt/bonanza/compose.yaml
# BONANZA_ENV_FILE=/opt/bonanza/.env
# BONANZA_IMAGES_ENV=/opt/bonanza/images.env
# BACKUP_ENV_FILE=/opt/bonanza/backup.env
